# Cloudflare Pages routing.
#
# /arcade is a client-side route: it exists only once React Router mounts, and
# there is no /arcade/index.html on disk. A static host asked for that path
# finds no file and serves its 404, so the easter egg is reachable by typing
# `idkfa` but NOT by opening the URL directly or reloading the page.
#
# The 200 is the whole point. A 302 to / would bounce the visitor to the cover
# and lose the path; a 200 rewrite serves the shell while the browser keeps the
# URL, so the router still sees /arcade and renders it.
#
# Static assets are matched before these rules, so /assets/* — including the
# hashed JS/CSS, the .jsdos bundle, og-cover.png and the résumé PDF — keep
# being served as themselves rather than falling through to the shell.
#
# Vite copies public/ verbatim into dist/, which puts this file at the root of
# the deployed output where Pages expects it.
/*  /index.html  200
